# armour/woman/padded_hang: the gambeson's short quilted skirt on the woman (the man's skirt under her hem rules) (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 27.2: T1's skirt is
# short): one stuffed row bulging past the seam, lit at the top-left, its hem a closed outline; it opens over the stride
# (wide) and trails in the run (flare). Finish regions: R the hem row, W a 2-pixel fray mark on the shadow side.
# Keys: the hang channel in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) the quilt softened: the lit side's seam rows a step up (8/7, not 8/6), so the T1 coat reads as stuffed
# cloth and not as bandage stripes; the shadow side keeps its flat step 1.
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1) T5-T6 skirt flare (STYLE_P2 29.3): `armour.t5` views facing D/U, 1 px more past the hips on the lower half; flared copies of the replace views go before them. Generated by FORGE-LIMBS flare.py.
use person
body woman
role armour padded
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
z 10
# (ladder i2, integration) her quilt in undyed linen (her tunic's apron is cloth3 buff, the man's gambeson colour): the T1
# coat reads as a coat over her tunic
legend 5 linen 0
legend 6 linen 1
legend 7 linen 2
legend 8 linen 3
legend 9 linen 4

